    "what": "Treating a language model not as an oracle but as something to interrogate. The recurring move is to take a prediction — a sentiment score — and make its *reasoning* legible: which tokens pushed the verdict which way, what happens if you swap a word, where the model is confident and where it guesses. Sentiment is the surface; the real subject is attribution and counterfactual exploration — running local inference (transformers.js) and ablating spans to render a heatmap over the text. It turns \"the model says 4 stars\" into \"here is *why*, and here is what would change it,\" and in doing so exposes the model's limits (sarcasm, mixed sentiment) as features rather than bugs.",
